tasks.prompt:
Add account deletion to the API (as started with `go run .`). `DELETE /api/user` deletes the account of the signed-in user and answers `200` or `204`; without a valid token it answers `401` and deletes nothing. After an account is deleted:
- `GET /api/profiles/{username}` for it answers `404`, logging in with its email and password answers `401`, and `GET /api/user` with a token issued to it answers `401`;
- the articles it wrote are gone: `GET /api/articles/{slug}` answers `404` for them, and they no longer appear in `GET /api/articles` (with or without filters) or in anybody's feed;
- the comments it wrote no longer appear in `GET /api/articles/{slug}/comments` of any article;
- its favorites are gone: they no longer count in any article's `favoritesCount`;
- the same username and email can be registered again, and the new account starts with no articles and no favorites;
- the data of every other account (its articles, comments, favorites, follows and profile) is unchanged.
All existing endpoints must keep working unchanged. Make sure the project's build, vet and tests still pass.
